== Deaths ==

The current state of the article says there were two deaths at the concert. However, I don't think this is straightforward. Current Wikipedia article content:

{{tq|A few hours after the concert, a 26-year-old Australian nurse fell  from railings after drinking heavily and taking MDMA. She sustained serious head injuries and died in hospital. Another man died on the beach after having a heart attack shortly after the concert.}} 

The consensus based on more recent sources seems to be 1) that the death of the nurse happened later, after the party had ended, and 2) the man died at home, not on the beach, and possibly was completely uninvolved in the event. [https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2002/jul/21/artsfeatures.features This 2002 Observer source] says:

{{tq|Most escaped unscathed, and '''reports of two deaths were wrong'''. One man died of a heart attack, not at the party but at home. And 25-year-old Australian nurse Karen Manders who had been at the party, hung around with her friends afterwards and fell from the esplanade in the early hours, according to sources.}}

What to do here? I think just reporting both accounts might be best — "According to X sources, people died, but according to Y sources, [qualifying information]." [[User:Popcornfud|Popcornfud]] ([[User talk:Popcornfud|talk]]) 23:31, 8 March 2025 (UTC)

