kind.post_text:
:::::Regarding this sentence:
:::::{{tq| In some places and at some times it has been cooked and served as [[street food]].}}
:::::Think about this logically. Is it possible for the dish to have been served as street food ''without'' this having happened in "some places" and at "some times"? This adds zero clarity. [[User:Popcornfud|Popcornfud]] ([[User talk:Popcornfud|talk]]) 07:27, 22 July 2025 (UTC)

:::We can get into the fine details of exactly which parts are important and which aren't -- and believe me, these kinds of debates are always super fun on Michael Jackson talk pages -- but I agree that the article is bloated. For example, looking at just the first sentence you edited:
:::{{tq|In early 1993, '''Michael''' Jackson befriended 13-year-old Jordan Chandler through Jordan's stepfather '''who became acquainted after Jackson had rented a vehicle'''.}}
:::Just "Jackson" here is fine, per [[MOS:SURNAME]], and the detail of how Jackson and the stepfather met doesn't seem important for this article. [[User:Popcornfud|Popcornfud]] ([[User talk:Popcornfud|talk]]) 17:52, 5 August 2025 (UTC)

::::::::{{tq|Point me to an article about a console which doesn’t use the North American name and the top picture isn’t the North American version of the console.}}
::::::::Think about this logically. Could there be another explanation for this? 
::::::::How many consoles whose names were changed for the western market used ''different'' names for North America and other western regions? [[User:Popcornfud|Popcornfud]] ([[User talk:Popcornfud|talk]]) 19:45, 9 January 2026 (UTC)

== Media reaction ==

{{tq|News media began covering the content of the FBI files after they were released on December 22, 2009. These outlets included The Guardian, USA Today, Variety, MTV, CNN, Billboard, ABC News, CBC News, BBC, France 24, and Reuters.}} 

What is the point of this sentence? If those sources have interesting/relevant things to say, then we can report what they say in the article. Merely saying that those sources exist is pointless.  We don't typically fill Wikipedia articles with lists of sources that ''exist'', we fill articles with ''content'' which we cite to sources. [[User:Popcornfud|Popcornfud]] ([[User talk:Popcornfud|talk]]) 19:50, 15 June 2026 (UTC)

